tagged-plain-value

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Tagged<T> captures a node's tag and then gives T the node without it, so an untagged enum or any Content-buffered type reads the plain value. Without it, Serde's Content buffer sees the tag again and reads the node as a one-key map {tag: value}.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream serde-saphyr gives the inner value of Tagged<T> the node without the synthetic tag map.
